  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating to see paint peeling, especially when you've just had your mobile home painted. Often, this happens because the surface wasn't prepped correctly. Think about it: if there's dirt, mildew, or old, loose paint still on the walls, new paint won't have a solid surface to grab onto. We always emphasize thorough washing and sometimes sanding to create a clean, slightly abraded surface. Another common culprit is skipping the primer or using the wrong type for your specific mobile home materials. Primer creates a bonding layer, and without it, or with an incompatible one, your finish coats are more likely to fail. Environmental factors can also play a role, like painting when it's too cold or humid, which prevents the paint from curing properly. Lastly, not all paints are created equal for mobile homes; some simply aren't designed to flex and breathe with the movement and temperature changes these homes experience. If you're seeing persistent peeling, it's a good sign that the underlying issue needs to be addressed professionally to ensure a long-lasting finish. We can help figure out what's really going on.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}